@page
@{
    Layout = null;
}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Fourth Coffee | Staff and kitchen</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/site.css" />
    <script src="/lib/msal/msal-browser.min.js" defer></script>
    <script src="/js/staff-entra.js" defer></script>
    <script src="/js/restaurant.js" defer></script>
</head>
<body data-workspace="staff">
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to main content</a>
<header><span class="brand">Fourth Coffee</span><nav aria-label="Workspaces">
    <a href="/">Guest journey</a><a href="/Staff" aria-current="page">Staff and kitchen</a>
</nav></header>
<main id="main">
    <p class="eyebrow">Restaurant operations</p><h1>Service, kitchen and floor coordination</h1>
    <p>Sign in with your assigned organizational account. Microsoft Entra API access tokens, staff roles
        and Floor.1 through Floor.5 permissions are verified server-side at both service boundaries.
        The public shell contains no visit or financial data. Sessions last at most 30 minutes,
        never beyond token expiry. There is no deployed synthetic password fallback.</p>
    <p id="notice" role="status" aria-live="polite">Authenticate to load your authorized workspace.</p>
    <form id="staff-session">
        <p>No role selector: permissions come from assigned Entra app roles.</p>
        <button type="submit">Sign in with Microsoft Entra</button>
    </form>
    <button id="staff-logout" type="button">Sign out</button>
    <p id="staff-identity" role="status"></p>
    <section><h2>Floor and kitchen board</h2>
        <label>Service date<input id="board-date" type="date" required /></label>
        <label>Meal turn<select id="board-turn"><option>1</option><option>2</option><option>3</option>
            <option>4</option><option>5</option></select></label>
        <label>Display floor<select id="floor-filter"><option value="">All authorized floors</option><option>1</option>
            <option>2</option><option>3</option><option>4</option><option>5</option></select></label>
        <label>Visit status<select id="status-filter"><option value="">All statuses</option>
            <option>Reserved</option><option>Active</option><option>Settled</option><option>Cancelled</option></select></label>
        <button id="board-refresh" type="button">Refresh board</button>
        <p>Connected boards refresh every two seconds. Pending dispatch is not kitchen acceptance.</p>
        <div id="board">No staff data loaded.</div>
    </section>
    <section><h2>Selected visit</h2><div id="visit">Select an authorized visit from the board.</div>
        <button id="refresh" type="button">Refresh selected visit</button>
        <button id="checkin" type="button" disabled>Preview check-in</button>
        <button id="cancel" type="button" disabled>Preview reservation cancellation</button>
        <button id="settle" type="button" disabled>Preview synthetic settlement</button>
        <p>Synthetic settlement - no money charged. Kitchen roles cannot view or settle bills.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="management-heading"><h2 id="management-heading">Manager reconciliation and recovery</h2>
        <p>Manager role required. Synthetic totals are not real payments. Missing DLQ evidence is not an empty queue.</p>
        <button id="management-refresh" type="button">Load manager evidence</button>
        <div id="management">No manager data loaded.</div>
        <form id="replay">
            <label>Dead-letter message ID<input name="messageId" maxlength="128" required /></label>
            <label>Ticket/session ID<input name="sessionId" maxlength="128" required /></label>
            <p>This explicit action queues an audited recovery request. It does not claim delivery or erase the inbox.</p>
            <button type="submit">Request this message replay</button>
        </form>
    </section>
    <section><h2>Review before confirming</h2><div id="previews">No pending action.</div></section>
    <section><h2>Service Coordinator</h2>
        <p>For kitchen-delay questions the Coordinator can invoke one bounded Kitchen Advisor.
            Recommendations never automatically reprioritize a ticket.</p>
        <form id="chat"><label>Ask about your authorized floors
            <textarea name="message" maxlength="2000" required></textarea></label>
            <button type="submit">Ask Coordinator</button></form>
        <div id="chat-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
    </section>
</main>
<footer>Fourth Coffee | Host: Hasan Ibrahimov | Kitchen: Nemanja Milatovic | Manager: Nino Kapanadze</footer>
</body>
</html>
